# Independent review: bounded deployment status polling

Verdict: no blocking finding in the reviewed polling scope. Exact reviewed source snapshots are under source/.

Compared poll.py, five tests and README with doc/spec/15-site.md's 600-second status-wait limit, failure/reconciliation requirements and the bounded transport contract. The public entry connects monotonic time, real sleep and the status transport. Each request receives at most ten seconds and at most the remaining wait. Only pending responses continue after up to five seconds of sleep. Unknown, terminal failure and transport failure stop without retry. Responses already received remain in the typed report. A success received at or after the deadline is retained but cannot return SUCCEEDED. No cancellation, deployment, journal write or LKG promotion occurs.

Independent execution: five repository tests passed normally and with Python -O, including deterministic full 600-second pending expiration. Additional probe.py checks 128 retained responses/requests under an intentionally stationary test clock, success just before/exactly at/after a one-second deadline, and public wait wiring through patched deterministic clock/sleep/status. Pending followed by a transport failure preserves the earlier response and receives request budgets of eight then three seconds. commands.json and raw outputs preserve all executions.

The 128-response test is a defensive-limit test with no-op test sleep; it is not a production timing scenario. With normal monotonic progress and five-second polling, the 600-second budget normally terminates earlier. No 600-second wall-clock run or real GitHub status request was performed. The subprocess transport's documented startup/termination/scheduling overhead still prevents a strict realtime guarantee; late replies are handled conservatively by the polling result.

This change provides bounded status observation only. SUCCEEDED remains one operation's outcome, not evidence of current public identity, smoke success, protected remote/journal agreement or immutable LKG. The reviewer made no implementation edits and does not infer publisher/recovery acceptance from these local tests.

All three source snapshots were additionally verified byte-for-byte against final commit 0a7d120.
